        "probe": "Map slots, clearance, exposed edge and pickup access with ruler/marker. Before fabrication verify strip bendability, bolt fit and pocket play <1 mm; abandon if geometry prevents capture. Using supplied strips/bolts/pads, build at most pocket and rival within 80 minutes. Observe within 20 minutes: up to three twenty-manual-stroke runs/configuration, ruler/stroke counter, displacement and qualitative seating pressure; spare in final run. Stopwatch up to three thick-gloved removal/return checks/configuration: <=60 seconds, no marked-edge contact. Optional pull-scale escape comparison <=10 N cannot establish resistance to unknown stroke forces. Stop for clearance intrusion or necessary edge contact.",
        "uncertainty": "Slot dimensions/locations must permit mounting outside clearance; supplied pliers must form sufficiently stiff strips; available bolts/strips must support capture/gloved gate. Stroke duration may limit informative comparisons; fewer runs reduce confidence. Hard constraints: no drilling, cutting, heating or gluing plate/carriage; keep 30 mm working edge exposed, added parts outside stroke clearance, carriage attached to rails."
